<title>SPAIN: Spain's Banesto cuts prime rate to 8.25 percent.</title>
<headline>Spain's Banesto cuts prime rate to 8.25 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Banco Espanol de Credito (Banesto), a unit of Banco Santander, said on Monday it had cut its prime rate to 8.25 percent from nine percent effective today.</p>
<p>It also said it would lower fixed-rate mortgage rates to 8.50 from 9.25 percent.</p>
<p>Consumer loan rates also fall 75 basis points to 11.75 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
